Rem AMCAF Blitter Copy with one to three sources, the limits, the minterms (the golden is the original's)
For N=0 To 3
Screen Open N,320,200,16,Lowres : Curs Off : Flash Off : Cls 0
Next N
Screen 0
For I=1 To 15 : Ink I : Circle 80+I*8,60+I*3,10+I*3 : Next I
Screen 1
For I=1 To 15 : Ink I : Bar I*20,I*10 To I*20+30,I*10+40 : Next I
Screen 2
For I=1 To 15 : Ink I : Draw 0,I*13 To 319,199-I*9 : Next I
Screen 3
Ink 7 : Bar 0,0 To 319,199
Blitter Copy Limit 3
DUMP[3]
Blitter Copy Limit 16,20 To 160,120
Blitter Copy 0,0 To 3,0
DUMP[3]
Blitter Copy 0,1 To 3,1,$0F
DUMP[3]
Blitter Copy 0,2 To 3,2,$F0
Blitter Copy 1,3 To 3,3,$FF
DUMP[3]
Blitter Copy Limit 0
Blitter Copy 0,0,1,0 To 3,0
Blitter Copy 0,1,1,1 To 3,1,$C0
Blitter Copy 0,2,1,2 To 3,2,$3C
DUMP[3]
Blitter Copy Limit 40,50 To 200,150
Blitter Copy 0,0,1,0,2,0 To 3,0
Blitter Copy 0,1,1,1,2,1 To 3,1,$E8
Blitter Copy 0,2,1,2,2,2 To 3,2,$96
Blitter Copy 0,3,1,3,2,3 To 3,3,$80
DUMP[3]
Blitter Copy Limit 0,0 To 320,200
Blitter Copy 2,0 To 3,0,$00
Blitter Copy 2,1 To 3,1,$0F
Blitter Copy 1,2 To 3,3
DUMP[3]
Print #1,"end"
Procedure DUMP[S]
 Blitter Wait
 For P=0 To 3
 For Y=0 To 199 Step 11
 C=0
 For X=0 To 38 Step 2
 C=C+Deek(Logbase(P)+Y*40+X)*(X+1)
 Next X
 Print #1,C;" ";
 Next Y
 Print #1,""
 Next P
End Proc
